From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: v8-embed-feedstock <noreply@github.com>
Date: Tue, 2 Sep 2026 00:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Do not assemble the embedded blob that becomes inline asm

With clang on Windows, mksnapshot writes the embedded builtins as
embedded.S in GNU assembler syntax (platform-embedded-file-writer-win.cc
picks MASM only for a compiler that is MSVC and not clang), and v8.gyp
already knows: under OS=="win" and clang==1 an action runs
asm_to_inline_asm.py over it and compiles the resulting embedded.cc.

But run_mksnapshot also marks its outputs process_outputs_as_sources, so
embedded.S stays a source of v8_snapshot, and gyp's ninja generator hands
every .S it sees on Windows to ml64:

  embedded.S(1) : error A2008:syntax error : /
  ...
  fatal error A1012:error count exceeds 100; stopping assembly

MSBuild never noticed because gyp's msvs generator files the .S as a
custom-build item with no tool, so it sits there inert.  The generators
add those outputs to the sources themselves, after the sources! exclusion
has been processed, so an exclusion cannot take it back out.  Instead the
sources are listed explicitly: snapshot.cc always, embedded.S everywhere
except the configuration that turns it into inline assembly.
---
 tools/v8_gypfiles/v8.gyp | 17 ++++++++++++++++-
 1 file changed, 16 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/tools/v8_gypfiles/v8.gyp b/tools/v8_gypfiles/v8.gyp
--- a/tools/v8_gypfiles/v8.gyp
+++ b/tools/v8_gypfiles/v8.gyp
@@ -385,6 +385,11 @@
       'toolsets': ['target'],
       'sources': [
         '<(V8_ROOT)/src/init/setup-isolate-deserialize.cc',
+        # Written by run_mksnapshot below.  Listed here rather than taken
+        # from the action's outputs so that embedded.S can be left out on
+        # the one configuration that does not assemble it (see the
+        # conditions at the end of this target).
+        '<(INTERMEDIATE_DIR)/snapshot.cc',
       ],
       'xcode_settings': {
         # V8 7.4 over macOS10.11 compatibility
@@ -417,7 +422,6 @@
             '<(INTERMEDIATE_DIR)/snapshot.cc',
             '<(INTERMEDIATE_DIR)/embedded.S',
           ],
-          'process_outputs_as_sources': 1,
           'conditions': [
             ['v8_random_seed', {
               'variables': {
@@ -506,6 +510,12 @@
             'abseil.gyp:abseil',
           ]
         }],
+        # With clang on Windows, mksnapshot writes embedded.S in GNU syntax,
+        # which ml64 cannot assemble; the action below turns it into inline
+        # assembly in a C++ file, and that is what gets compiled.  Everywhere
+        # else embedded.S is assembled as it is.  gyp's ninja generator hands
+        # every .S in the sources to ml64, so on the clang configuration the
+        # .S must not be a source at all -- MSBuild merely ignored it.
         ['OS=="win" and clang==1', {
           'actions': [
             {
@@ -526,6 +536,10 @@
               ],
             },
           ],
+        }, {
+          'sources': [
+            '<(INTERMEDIATE_DIR)/embedded.S',
+          ],
         }],
       ],
     },  # v8_snapshot
